  "description": "methodology 1.8 — an opening learning-rate ramp on the shipped fit: both rates scaled linearly from near zero up to the schedule over the first R epochs, multiplied into the decay so the cosine itself is untouched. The sweep is over the LENGTH, R in {0, 250, 500, 1000} — 0 being the schedule with no ramp — and it exists because a four-seed reading of R=500 on the axis_space panel came out better on every seed by 1.3 mnat with an interval spanning zero: an effect the size of the run-to-run spread, which four seeds cannot resolve and one length cannot bracket. EIGHT SEEDS PER LENGTH, at one pinned held-out draw (split_seed 0) and one pinned feature basis (pca_seed 0), so every arm is scored on the same problems and the difference between two lengths at one seed is the ramp alone; eight is what 80% power at the observed effect asks for. THE BEST LENGTH MUST BE INTERIOR: a sweep whose winner is its longest point has found a boundary, not an optimum, and the panel is extended with longer ramps until the level turns — the producer refuses to name a shipping length otherwise. What a ramp may not do is move the axes: the same arms are read for cross-seed identity and for agreement with the taught rule ends, so a level bought at the price of the basis would show.",
